        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758293,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The MSX is a standardized home computer architecture, born from Microsoft's involvement but finding its greatest popularity outside the United States, particularly in Asia, South America, and Europe. Before the rise of the Nintendo Family Computer, it was a key platform for major Japanese game studios like Konami and Hudson Soft, hosting the original *Metal Gear* series. \n\nA diverse library of games flourished on the MSX, including classics like *Antarctic Adventure*, *Bomberman*, *Parodius*, and *Puyo Puyo*.  It also saw versions of popular titles such as *Castlevania*, *Contra*, *Dragon Quest*, and *Final Fantasy*.  Years later, efforts to revive the platform included the MSX Mini Replica, a faithful reproduction, and the official MSXPLAYer emulator.  Notably, Nintendo even brought MSX games to the Wii and Wii U Virtual Console in Japan."
          },
